{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwbErMXZZuWD2hAYauYa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't confirmed that the rule actually fires on 5xx traffic. Its status was still \"pending\" right after creation.\n\n**What the data holds:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` has one document per web request, with these key fields:\n- `timestamp` (the data view's time field)\n- `response` (a string status code, so 5xx has to be matched as text)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `url`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-7ebd7128 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Bytes by file extension (bar chart)\n\nIt is at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-7ebd7128-web-logs-overview-fdc2a8ea86cc.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-7ebd7128 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule (`.es-query`) that runs every minute.\n- **Condition:** it fires when more than 10 documents in the last 5 minutes have a `response.keyword` matching `5[0-9][0-9]`.\n- **Actions:** I didn't attach any action connector, so a firing will show up as an alert in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere.\n- **Sample data:** the sample logs are historical, so the rule may not fire unless new 5xx documents are indexed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1281,"cache_read_input_tokens":19096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1281},"output_tokens":524,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"5cde7569-b31a-4366-95b7-